#exercise[
  Let $E = M_n (R)$, where $R$ is a commutative ring and $n >= 1$. Let $Lambda$
  be an $R$-algebra, and $Gamma = E times.o_R Lambda tilde.equiv M_n (Lambda)$.
  Show that the isomorphism $Pic_R Lambda tilde.equiv Pic_R Gamma$ given in
  #source(347)@th:morita-picard, arising from the Morita equivalence of $Lambda$
  and $Gamma$ over $R$, is also given by the map
  $
    (X) -> (E times.o_R X), quad (X) in Pic_R Lambda.
  $
  #hint[@exc:matrix-picard-iso][Let $L = R^((n)) times.o_R Lambda$, viewed as
    bimodule $lmodule(Gamma, L)_Lambda$ after identifying $Gamma$ with
    $Hom_Lambda (L, L)$. Let $L^(-1) = Hom_Lambda (L, Lambda)$, viewed as
    $(Lambda, Gamma)$-bimodule. By @th:morita-picard, the map defined by
    $
      (X) -> (L times.o_Lambda X times.o_Lambda L^(-1)), quad
      (X) in Pic_R Lambda,
    $
    gives an isomorphism $Pic_R Lambda tilde.equiv Pic_R Gamma$. However, there
    are two-sided $Gamma$-isomorphisms
    $
      L times.o_Lambda X times.o_Lambda L^(-1)
      & tilde.equiv Hom_Lambda (L, L times.o_Lambda X) \
      & tilde.equiv Hom_Lambda (Lambda^((n)), X^((n)))
      tilde.equiv E times.o_R X.
    $
    Therefore $(L times.o_Lambda X times.o_Lambda L^(-1)) = (E times.o_R X)$ in
    $Pic_R Gamma$.] <hint:matrix-picard-iso>
] <exc:matrix-picard-iso>

